// Signing for debug builds, the ones run from Xcode.
//
// Out of the box a debug build is signed to run on this Mac only, so it can't share albums: its sharing sheet says
// why. To share albums from Xcode, sign it with a team that has the App ID com.pugglesoft.PugglePhotos with iCloud
// (CloudKit, with the container iCloud.com.pugglesoft.PugglePhotos) and Push Notifications: put these three lines,
// with the team's ID, in Config/Signing.xcconfig, which Git ignores, and add an Apple ID in that team to Xcode's
// Accounts settings. Xcode then makes the certificate and provisioning profile itself.
//
//     DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = ABCDE12345
//     CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY = Apple Development
//     CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS = Config/iCloud.entitlements
//
// iCloud.entitlements is PugglePhotos/PugglePhotos.entitlements with iCloud's added, so keep the two alike.
//
// Debug builds use iCloud's production environment, the one installed copies use, so an album shared from Xcode
// reaches people who installed PugglePhotos, and theirs reach it. Production only takes the kinds of records its
// schema already has. When PugglePhotos starts saving a new kind (and once at the start, for iCloud's own record of
// a share), add this line to Signing.xcconfig, share an album, deploy the development schema to production in
// CloudKit Console, then take the line out again:
//
//     ICLOUD_ENVIRONMENT = Development

CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY = -
CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS = PugglePhotos/PugglePhotos.entitlements
ICLOUD_ENVIRONMENT = Production

#include? "Signing.xcconfig"
